# Spectra host and AI boundary
- Follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/LLM_CONTRACT.md`. Active prompt/adapters are in
  `extension/providers.ts` and `extension/cursor.ts`; session/commands are in `extension/extension.ts`.
- No Express/API proxy or environment-file credentials. Keys are entered in native password
  prompts and stored only in VS Code SecretStorage; never emit them to webview, files or logs.
- Require workspace trust for source, keys, live calls and exports; confirm source transmission
  natively before each call. Direct API keys are separate from explicit Cursor CLI login.
- Cursor CLI uses the dedicated Spectra configuration, temporary workspace, denied tools, stdin context,
  bounded subprocess and shared result validation described in `docs/LLM_CONTRACT.md`. No implicit
  editor credentials or automatic repository edits. CLI history is separate from panel session state.
- Capture current selection/document including unsaved text; max 60,000 chars. No crawling imports.
  Keep source Uri private; guard local workspace/file boundaries and obvious sensitive paths.
- Runtime-validate allowlisted commands and IDs. Resolve exact source variants in host state.
- Generate: no selected sources, exactly three directions. First custom-source call also returns
  original reconstruction; subsequent calls must not replace the fixed original.
- Refine: one exact selected implementation → one result; remix: exactly two distinct IDs → one.
- Implementations have name, hypothesis, changes, html, css, js. Assign IDs in the host;
  validate field types/counts/sizes/nonblank content and entire candidate state before committing.
- Preserve source facts/billing units; no genuine-looking invented proof. Request concise hypotheses,
  not hidden reasoning. Palette-only alternatives do not satisfy live generation requirements.
- Output self-contained responsive HTML/CSS/vanilla JS, not React, external assets or network calls.
- One mutation at a time; 90-second live timeout, bounded responses and cancellable notification.
  Abort on panel disposal; always release busy state. No automatic retries or fallback fixtures.
- Keep prior canvas/selection on malformed, truncated, refused, cancelled or failed responses.
- Errors must be actionable without vendor bodies, keys, authorization headers or sensitive source.
- Tests with mocked fetch/VS Code do not prove real SecretStorage, editor CSP or vendor availability.
